From 9713a19487bb7d9d32486e36fc76279a6cbd4ec2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:41:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper: Policy Routing swaps its rules in place, the DNS
 health check holds while the uplink is down, a slewed first clock sync
 counts, the firewall chains are signed and watched

Policy Routing (rc/reaper_pbr.c): a rebuild no longer tears down first. The
new rules are built under the other chain name (REAPER_PBR <-> REAPER_PBR_N),
the PREROUTING jump is replaced in place (-R), the old chain is dropped and the
new one renamed (-E). Routing rules are kept or added first and only stale
fwmark-form rules are deleted afterwards, so live tunnel flows never see a
rules-free window. Full teardown stays on the disable path only. The fwsim kick
after an apply is dedented; it always ran after either apply.

DNS health check (rc/rdnshc.c): a miss is not counted while the uplink is known
down (link_wan 0, or wan0_state_t set and not 2); hits always count; one HOLD
and one back line per transition. Boxes without those keys are never held.
Each WAN blip used to cost a failover, a re-apply, a restore and two extra
dnsmasq reloads.

Clock (rc/ntpd.c): busybox ntpd slews a clock that is already within a second
(amtm RouterDate pre-sets it), and the hook honoured "step" only, so ntp_ready
stayed 0 and everything gated on it (WireGuard, OpenVPN, cron, add-ons) waited.
A stratum or periodic event with 0 < stratum < 16 now counts as the first sync
and logs "Initial clock set (slewed: ...)".

Firewall chains (rc/reaper_fw.c, rc/rwatch.c): apply.sh signs REAPER_FWI/F/O
and the nat FWM chain (md5 of -S) into /tmp/reaper_fw/chainsig; rwatch 3f
recomputes it, and two ticks of mismatch re-apply the committed apply.sh under
the firewall lock, 600 s apart, at most twice, never while a candidate is
armed. FWN/FWHC stay unsigned.

rwatch also: the incident bundle takes dmesg and a 300-line syslog tail right
after summary.txt, before its own fcctl/bpmctl dumps push the trigger out; the
syslog mirror rotates at 8 MB before appending, not after.

rc/lan.c: stop_lan logs the radio-off line only for a wl* name (eth1-eth4 were
logged as radios). rc/init.c: the one-time DTIM default runs before start_lan
(the function itself is in services.c, with the destination-names commit).

reaper_fwsim: witness row A1b, the WAN masquerade, with a $NAT placeholder from
wanN_nat_x (n/a when NAT is off).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
